# direnv entry point — auto-activates the Nix devShell on `cd`.
#
# One-time setup per developer:
#   1. Install direnv (https://direnv.net) and hook it into your shell.
#   2. (Recommended) Install nix-direnv for fast, cached shell entry:
#        https://github.com/nix-community/nix-direnv
#   3. Run `direnv allow` in this directory once.
#
# Not using direnv? Just run `nix develop` manually — same result.
use flake

# Personal, per-developer layer: gitignored ./.envrc.local (auto-created by
# devshell-init from .envrc.local.example). Kept AFTER `use flake` so editing
# it reloads direnv without invalidating nix-direnv's flake cache. Things like
# NVIM_LANGS (which editor features to load) live there, not here — .envrc is
# the shared project entry point.
source_env_if_exists .envrc.local
